WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.282
Duplicate detection and duplicate resolution are different stages.

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:08.067
Detection tries to find plausible candidate groups.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.967
Resolution decides what to do with them.

00:00:10.967 --> 00:00:17.347
That could mean choosing a survivor, merging complementary fields, quarantining the group,

00:00:17.347 --> 00:00:19.642
or sending it for human review.

00:00:19.642 --> 00:00:23.617
Separating the stages makes deduplication safer.

00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:31.177
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:31.177 --> 00:00:37.282
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.282 --> 00:00:45.577
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:51.667
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:57.733
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
